    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="1034" n="934" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg934"/>

                <head>No. 590.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay
                        to Mr. Stevens.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 29,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 71.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 67, transmitting the result of your presentation to His Majesty’s Government
                    of the considerations contained in the circular instruction of August last,
                    touching the prevention of an emigration to this country from foreign parts of
                    persons intending to join the Mormon community in Utah, and in reply to request
                    that you will express to His Majesty’s Government the appreciation of the
                    Government of the United States of the action taken by it in the direction
                    referred to.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN HAY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
